<p>Earth trapped a record amount of heat in 2025, the United Nations&#x27; World Meteorological Organization said in its annual State of the Global Climate report released Monday. The agency also said the 11 hottest years ever recorded all came between 2015 and 2025, and that 2025 was the second- or third-warmest year on record at about 1.43 degrees Celsius above the 1850-1900 average.</p><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>World Meteorological Organization: The agency says Earth&#x27;s climate system is becoming increasingly unbalanced, with rising greenhouse gas emissions driving the trend. (<a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202603230089.html'>AllAfrica</a>)</li><li>United Nations climate agencies: Their warning stresses that the effects of record heat trapped by the planet could last for thousands of years, making this a long-term problem as well as an immediate one. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/planet-trapped-record-heat-2025-un'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>South China Morning Post: Its coverage described the new WMO findings as a &#x27;flashing red&#x27; warning, underscoring the urgency international bodies attach to the trend. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/article/3347542/flashing-red-un-alarmed-heat-trapped-earth-hits-record-high'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/planet-trapped-record-heat-2025-un'>Planet trapped record heat in 2025: UN</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/article/3347542/flashing-red-un-alarmed-heat-trapped-earth-hits-record-high'>‘Flashing red’: UN alarmed as heat trapped by Earth hits record high</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202603230089.html'>Africa: Earth Records Hottest 11-Year Period As Climate Crisis Deepens - WMO</a> - allafrica.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/environment/article/2026/03/23/earth-trapped-record-amount-of-heat-in-2025-un-